{"tool_name":"scasa","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"scasa","home":"https://github.com/eudoraleer/scasa","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Isoform-level Quantification for Single-Cell RNA Sequencing.","addition_date":"2022-05-17T17:27:22.194518Z","last_update_date":"2022-05-17T17:27:22.197133Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:scasa","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"trungnghia.vu@ki.se","name":"Trung Nghia Vu","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7945-5750","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Huy Q Dinh"},{"name":"Lu Pan"},{"name":"Yudi Pawitan"}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://github.com/eudoraleer/Scasa_Paper/wiki"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Gene expression profiling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0314"},{"term":"Quantification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3799"},{"term":"Read mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3198"}]}],"name":"Scasa","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/BIOINFORMATICS/BTAB807","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 The Author(s) 2021. Published by Oxford University Press.Motivation: RNA expression at isoform level is biologically more informative than at gene level and can potentially reveal cellular subsets and corresponding biomarkers that are not visible at gene level. However, due to the strong 3' bias sequencing protocol, mRNA quantification for high-throughput single-cell RNA sequencing such as Chromium Single Cell 3' 10\u00d7 Genomics is currently performed at the gene level. Results: We have developed an isoform-level quantification method for high-throughput single-cell RNA sequencing by exploiting the concepts of transcription clusters and isoform paralogs. The method, called Scasa, compares well in simulations against competing approaches including Alevin, Cellranger, Kallisto, Salmon, Terminus and STARsolo at both isoform- and gene-level expression. The reanalysis of a CITE-Seq dataset with isoform-based Scasa reveals a subgroup of CD14 monocytes missed by gene-based methods.","authors":[{"name":"Dinh H.Q."},{"name":"Pan L."},{"name":"Pawitan Y."},{"name":"Vu T.N."}],"date":"2022-03-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"Isoform-level quantification for single-cell RNA sequencing"},"pmcid":"PMC8826380","pmid":"34864849"}],"topic":[{"term":"Biomarkers","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3360"},{"term":"Gene expression","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0203"},{"term":"Gene transcripts","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3512"},{"term":"RNA-Seq","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3170"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"Scasa","home":"https://bio.tools/scasa","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Isoform-level Quantification for Single-Cell RNA Sequencing.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:scasa/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":null,"interpreted":true,"license":null,"public":true,"readme":false,"repository":{"anonymous":null,"online":null}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"manual":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":14,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2022"},{"count":2,"year":"2023"},{"count":2,"year":"2026"},{"count":4,"year":"2025"},{"count":5,"year":"2024"}],"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btab807","pmcid":"PMC8826380","pmid":"34864849","ref_count":0,"refs":[],"title":"Isoform-level quantification for single-cell RNA sequencing.","year":2022}]}],"readme":false,"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false